<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Empire of Vietnam</h1><p class="st-meta">1945 CE – 1945 CE · capital Hue</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short-lived Japanese-backed Vietnamese state proclaimed by Emperor Bao Dai after Japan ousted the French in March 1945.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 9 March 1945 Japanese forces overthrew the French administration across <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/french-indochina">French Indochina</a>. On 11 March Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a>, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan's</a> urging, declared the treaties of protection with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> void and proclaimed the independence of the Empire of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam">Vietnam</a>, covering <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-of-annam">Annam</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-of-tonkin">Tonkin</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a> appointed a cabinet of non-communist intellectuals under the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tran-trong-kim">Tran Trong Kim</a>, which reintroduced Vietnamese as the language of administration, revised school curricula and negotiated the return of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-cochinchina">Cochinchina</a> and the cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiphong">Haiphong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/da-nang">Da Nang</a> from Japanese control. Its power was limited by the Japanese military and by the famine then devastating the north.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan's</a> surrender, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> launched the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/august-revolution">August Revolution</a> and seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bao Dai</a> announced his abdication on 25 August 1945 and handed his seal and sword to Viet Minh representatives on 30 August; on 2 September <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh">Ho Chi Minh</a> declared the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/democratic-republic-of-vietnam">Democratic Republic of Vietnam</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/empire-of-vietnam.jpg" alt="Empire of Vietnam" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Smurrayinchester · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Long_tinh_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1945 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hue</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bao Dai, Tran Trong Kim</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Confucianism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Vietnamese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Đế quốc Việt Nam</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1945&amp;focus=empire-of-vietnam" aria-label="Empire of Vietnam on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7610 1566 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Empire of Vietnam lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7930 1822L7930 1822M7930 1822L8529 1145M7930 1822L7846 1656"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7930 1822h0M8529 1145h0M7846 1656h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7930 1822h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7930 1822h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Hue. <a href="/atlas?year=1945&amp;focus=empire-of-vietnam">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
